<Layout title="Membership | Kin & Campus" description="August through May. Visits in town, a number they can text, and a note home when the plan changes. Membership is not insurance.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Membership</div><h1>A seat for the school year.</h1><p class="lead">August through May. Visits in Blacksburg, a number they can text, and a note to the hometown doctor when the plan changes.</p></div>
<div class="w">
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>The year</h3><p>One student, August through May. We keep the panel small enough that we can usually see them the same week, and often the same day.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Inside the year</h3><p>Office visits in town. A number they can text. Check-ins after breaks and around finals. Refills that do not lapse. Forms for school, housing, sports, and travel. A video visit when they do not need a room. A note to the hometown doctor if the plan changes.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Outside the year</h3><p>The ER, the hospital, a specialist, and advanced imaging are not part of membership. We help arrange those. Keep their primary insurance for labs, specialists, and hospital care. This website is not a chart.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">When they should start with us</div>
<p class="lead">If it is a true emergency, call 911. For a fever, an asthma flare, or an allergy that a local pediatrician can handle, they can write us first. We already know their baseline.</p>

<h2 style="margin:48px 0 20px">Questions parents ask</h2>
<details><summary>How does it start?</summary><p>A parent usually writes first. We set up a call. Once they join, the student meets us in Blacksburg before classes get loud. After that, the number is theirs.</p></details>
<details><summary>How soon can they be seen?</summary><p>The same week, and usually the same day. The panel stays small so that remains true during exams.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you share my student's information with me?</summary><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. Before we start, we write down what they want you to hear, and we follow it. If the plan changes, their hometown doctor gets a note that afternoon.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does this replace insurance?</summary><p>No. Membership is not insurance. Keep their primary coverage for hospitalizations, emergency care, specialists, and labs.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if my student is away from Blacksburg?</summary><p>In-person care here is the core of the practice. If they do not need a room, we can do a video visit.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if it's an emergency?</summary><p>Call 911 or go to the nearest emergency room. Once they are safe, tell us. We will pick up the follow-up from there.</p></details>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></p>
</div>
</Layout>
